 "about": "A membership chain (regalia.membership/v3, epochs 1 and 2) signed by a P-256 root on a real Nitrokey HSM 2, so a verifier is checked against card-made signatures, not only software ones (#156, #293). Epoch 1 was signed in process through authority.Pkcs11Signer; epoch 2 by `python3 -m deploy.baremetal.manifest sign` (typed confirmation). Both are CKM_ECDSA over SHA-256 of DOMAIN || canonical(manifest), r||s, low-S. Epoch 1 names a typed revocation key (a software test key, public only). Public keys are written by composition, as in typed-keys-p256.json: the pinned root as \"root_public\"; a typed entry as {\"alg\", \"public\"} (the reader restores \"key\"); each envelope's signing key as \"signature_public\", put back into signature.key. Expected: the chain is accepted from root_public, epoch 2.",
